WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.022 --> 00:00:10.783
Farming might not seem like a high-tech business.

2
00:00:11.684 --> 00:00:15.325
Farmers plant seeds, water them, and let the plants grow.

3
00:00:16.246 --> 00:00:20.627
Then the crops are harvested, and the food eventually gets to our tables.

4
00:00:21.488 --> 00:00:26.010
But thanks to genetic engineering, farming has become high-tech.

5
00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:31.372
With genetic engineering, scientists can change the genes of living things.

6
00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:38.186
This technology lets scientists create plants and animals that better meet the needs of humans.

7
00:00:39.006 --> 00:00:46.153
Genes control the characteristics of living things, determining features such as color, size, and appearance.

8
00:00:48.815 --> 00:00:52.679
Scientists have learned a lot about modifying genes in recent years.

9
00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:58.164
But humans have actually been modifying plants and animals for much longer.

10
00:00:59.196 --> 00:01:05.742
Early cultures bred animals with useful traits, hoping the animals' offspring would inherit these traits.

11
00:01:06.602 --> 00:01:09.064
This process is called selective breeding.

12
00:01:10.025 --> 00:01:16.150
Using it, humans produced stronger and faster horses, as well as sheep with more wool.

13
00:01:17.311 --> 00:01:21.115
Selective breeding also created new types of fruits and vegetables.

14
00:01:23.397 --> 00:01:27.280
Even many popular dog breeds are the product of selective breeding.

15
00:01:28.124 --> 00:01:32.026
Selective breeding works well, but it's slow and limited.

16
00:01:32.967 --> 00:01:38.530
Modern genetic engineering is faster and lets scientists achieve many more results.

17
00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:43.933
Scientists can change a species' characteristics by editing its genes.

18
00:01:44.733 --> 00:01:51.957
This can mean deleting genes that control unwanted characteristics or transferring genes from another species.

19
00:01:52.818 --> 00:01:58.145
An organism, or living thing, that is modified this way is known as a GMO.

20
00:01:58.965 --> 00:02:02.406
GMO stands for genetically modified organism.

21
00:02:04.687 --> 00:02:07.269
GMOs can be used to help the environment.

22
00:02:08.369 --> 00:02:14.412
For example, scientists are working on modifying pigs to produce less pollution from their poop.

23
00:02:18.333 --> 00:02:21.895
Another GMO is a tree modified for papermaking.

24
00:02:23.035 --> 00:02:27.629
Making paper from this tree requires fewer chemicals and less energy.

25
00:02:28.909 --> 00:02:33.531
Genetic engineering is a big help to farmers growing crops for food as well.

26
00:02:34.331 --> 00:02:40.473
Scientists have found a way to protect bananas from a deadly disease by using a gene found in

27
00:02:40.513 --> 00:02:41.334
green peppers.

28
00:02:42.374 --> 00:02:44.955
This gene protects the peppers from the disease.

29
00:02:45.815 --> 00:02:48.376
Scientists can transfer the gene to bananas.

30
00:02:49.292 --> 00:02:52.773
The modified bananas are then resistant to the disease.

31
00:02:53.473 --> 00:02:56.874
GMO crops can also be made resistant to insects.

32
00:02:57.814 --> 00:03:01.295
Farmers don't have to use as many pesticides with these crops.

33
00:03:02.276 --> 00:03:06.277
This is a big advantage for farmers who can't afford pesticides.

34
00:03:07.177 --> 00:03:10.458
It also lets farmers avoid using dangerous chemicals.

35
00:03:11.358 --> 00:03:14.479
And that keeps more chemicals out of the environment.

36
00:03:15.439 --> 00:03:18.240
In many places in the world, water is limited.

37
00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:22.943
Scientists can create GMO crops that need less water.

38
00:03:24.024 --> 00:03:27.747
Other crops can be designed to produce more food on less land.

39
00:03:28.667 --> 00:03:33.331
This could help feed the world's growing population without using more land.

40
00:03:34.252 --> 00:03:36.253
GMOs have health benefits as well.

41
00:03:36.954 --> 00:03:40.937
Scientists have engineered beef cattle that are resistant to disease.

42
00:03:42.258 --> 00:03:44.960
Other foods can be engineered to have more nutrients.

43
00:03:46.572 --> 00:03:51.736
And GMOs can even be used to make medicines more effective and less expensive.

44
00:03:53.697 --> 00:03:59.261
With genetic engineering, many things can be improved and the possibilities are endless.

45
00:04:01.002 --> 00:04:07.427
All scientists need are the right genes to make longer-lasting, better-tasting, and more nutritious foods.

46
00:04:09.368 --> 00:04:14.472
This sounds like great news, but genetic engineering is still a new technology.

47
00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:17.881
Its consequences aren't completely understood.

48
00:04:18.681 --> 00:04:20.482
GMOs could pose risks.

49
00:04:21.382 --> 00:04:24.163
People might develop allergies to GMO foods.

50
00:04:25.323 --> 00:04:28.924
GMOs themselves could also show unexpected results.

51
00:04:29.844 --> 00:04:34.166
They could grow faster or slower, or differently than expected.

52
00:04:35.486 --> 00:04:39.047
GMO crops could spread their genes to other plants in the wild.

53
00:04:39.867 --> 00:04:42.208
This could cause changes in the environment.

54
00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:46.041
Many people are opposed to GMOs for these reasons.

55
00:04:46.881 --> 00:04:52.223
Some countries have completely banned them, while others have laws that control their use.

56
00:04:53.003 --> 00:04:56.064
In many places GMOs must be clearly labeled.

57
00:04:57.964 --> 00:05:03.286
Even in countries where they are allowed, local governments sometimes write laws to ban them.

58
00:05:04.246 --> 00:05:07.627
Many people will only buy food labeled non-GMO.

59
00:05:08.407 --> 00:05:12.188
These people often oppose GMOs for reasons beyond safety.

60
00:05:13.084 --> 00:05:17.068
Some believe it is wrong for humans to change nature in this way.

61
00:05:18.069 --> 00:05:24.114
Or they worry that companies who own GMOs will have too much control over the world's food supply.

62
00:05:24.975 --> 00:05:28.158
So far the GMOs that have been developed seem safe.

63
00:05:28.938 --> 00:05:32.401
GMOs have the potential to be a great benefit to humans.

64
00:05:33.162 --> 00:05:36.805
But they also have the potential to create future problems.

65
00:05:37.726 --> 00:05:43.447
There is still a long way to go before the technology and its effects are fully understood.
